Use the Generated Bindings in the High-Level Language: Once you have the shared library (_mymath.so), you can use it directly in your high-level language like Python. Example Python Code: import mymath #Use the C++ function through Python
result = mymath.add(5, 3)
print(f"Result from C++ code: {result}") Java Example (JNI): public class ComplexMath { static { System.loadLibrary("mymath"); } public native double computeSqrt(double x);
} MyMath cm = new MyMath();
double result = cm.computeSqrt(16);
System.out.println("Result from C++: " + result);
